EXT. THE FIELD - NIGHT #15#

Amos unyokes the oxen by moonlight in the far field. Up the hill, music. He stops with the yoke in his hands.

Dan comes running down the path with a torch.

AMOS
Dan. What is this?

DAN
Your brother is come; and your father has killed the fatted calf, because he has him back safe and sound.

Amos stands very still.

EXT. ELIAB'S FARM - GATE - NIGHT

Amos stops at the edge of the lamp's light. Through the open house door: the dancing, the fires, the robe. He doesn't take another step.

INT. ELIAB'S HOUSE - CONTINUOUS

Dan pushes through the dancers to Eliab.

DAN
He will not come in.

Asher rises.

ASHER
Let me go out to him.

ELIAB
Stay. I will bring your brother in.

EXT. ELIAB'S FARM - GATE - CONTINUOUS

Eliab comes out to Amos. Warm light behind the father; the cold night behind the son.

ELIAB
Come in, son. Your place is set beside mine.

AMOS
You stood at the gate for him.

AMOS
You made Nahum pay him full weight for our grandfather's vines.

Amos's eyes go to his father's bare finger.

AMOS
Is the ring on his hand?

ELIAB
It is.

AMOS
Many years have I laboured in your service, Father, and never once have I turned from your word.

AMOS
Yet not one kid of the flock was ever given me, that I might make merry with my friends.

Behind them, in the house, the music falters and stops. Faces turn toward the door.

AMOS
But now this son of yours is come, who has wasted your substance among harlots,

In the doorway behind his father, Asher, in the robe, flinches at the word, and does not move.

AMOS
and for him you have slain the fatted calf!

Eliab does not step back. He takes Amos's hand in both of his.

ELIAB
Son, you are ever with me, and all that is mine is yours.

ELIAB
Yet it was fitting that we should make merry and be glad.

Amos pulls his hand free.

ELIAB
For this brother of yours was dead, and lives again. He was lost, and is found.

In the doorway, Asher holds out the sling his brother made him.

Amos looks at it. His jaw sets. He doesn't move.

Eliab's hands stay open between them.

CUT TO:

